  "base_remarks": [
    "MATH-125 (Calculus I) is omitted from the plan: MATH-126 (Calculus II) and MATH-226 (Calculus III) are already in the completed timeline, which transitively proves MATH-125 was satisfied. Placing it now would serve no scheduling purpose.",
    "GE-C and GE-G are merged into a single 4-unit slot in Semester 1 using the GE-G double-dip rule — GE-G (Global Perspectives I) can be satisfied by a course that also satisfies a Core Literacy category (GE-C), saving one 4-unit slot across the plan.",
    "CSCI-401 (Capstone) is placed in Semester 2 (the final semester) per capstone timing rules; CSCI-310 is placed in Semester 1 to satisfy its prerequisite one semester earlier.",
    "CSCI-485 (File and Database Management) is selected as the top-ranked elective (score 1.0) to satisfy the 4-unit upper-division elective budget; all prereqs are already in the completed timeline.",
    "TAC-303 (Full-Stack Web Development) is placed in Semester 2 as enrichment — it is the top-ranked enrichment course (score 1.0) and directly aligns with the backend engineering career goal. Its prereq (CSCI-103) is in the completed timeline, so no enabler placement is needed. TAC-405 (Advanced Back-End Web Development), which requires TAC-303, cannot fit in the same semester and is excluded due to insufficient remaining semesters."
  ],
