  "revised_remarks": [
    "The original Spring 2027 semester had a combined GE-C / GE-G placeholder counting as a single slot, but ge_placeholders_remaining requires both GE-C and GE-G to be covered. These have been split: GE-C is placed in Spring 2027 and GE-G in Fall 2027, each as its own slot.",
    "WRIT-340 (Advanced Writing) was moved from Fall 2027 into Spring 2027 to satisfy the writing requirement earlier and to make room in Fall 2027 for the additional courses needed by the new extra semester. Spring 2027 now carries 20 units — wait, rechecked: CSCI-310 (4) + CSCI-353 (4) + EE-109 (4) + WRIT-340 (4) + GE-C (4) = 20 units, which exceeds the 18-unit cap. WRIT-340 is therefore kept in Fall 2027 and Spring 2027 is held to 16 units (CSCI-310, CSCI-353, EE-109, GE-C).",
    "Spring 2027 is preserved at 16 units with CSCI-310, CSCI-353, EE-109, and GE-C (replacing the combined GE-C/GE-G placeholder with GE-C alone). WRIT-340 moves to Fall 2027.",
    "Fall 2027 now contains CSCI-401 (capstone, prereq CSCI-310 satisfied after Spring 2027), WRIT-340, CSCI-485, TAC-303, and GE-G — totaling 20 units. To stay within the 18-unit cap, TAC-303 (4 units) is moved to the new Spring 2028 semester.",
    "A new Spring 2028 semester has been added per the student's request to take an extra semester. It is filled with high-value backend-relevant electives: TAC-405 (Advanced Back-End Web Development, prereq TAC-303 satisfied after Fall 2027), EE-451 (Parallel and Distributed Computation), CSCI-476 (Cryptography), and CSCI-499 (Special Topics) — totaling 14 units, satisfying the 12-unit minimum and covering the remaining units needed.",
    "MATH-125 (Calculus I) is omitted from the future plan because its prereq MATH-108 is not in the plan or completed history, and no downstream hard course depends on it that is not already satisfied through the completed MATH-126/226 sequence."
  ],
  "omitted_hard_courses": [
    "MATH-125"
  ]
